exercises.solution:
The dependencies are `(student_id, course_code) → grade` and `course_code → course_title`. The second has a left-hand side that is only *part* of the key, so the title is repeated for every student who takes the course. That is a second-normal-form violation: renaming "Databases" to "Data Systems" means updating hundreds of rows, and if one is missed the table contradicts itself. The fix is to split it:

```sql
CREATE TABLE courses (course_code TEXT PRIMARY KEY, course_title TEXT NOT NULL);
CREATE TABLE enrolments (
  student_id  INTEGER NOT NULL,
  course_code TEXT NOT NULL REFERENCES courses(course_code),
  grade       TEXT,
  PRIMARY KEY (student_id, course_code)
);
```

